WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.640 --> 00:00:06.020
Hello, and welcome to your second drink of Job Fair.

2
00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:12.660
We had a lot to say in this episode about washing our hands, blisters, and golf courses.

3
00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:14.620
Such a weird liSt.

4
00:00:15.520 --> 00:00:20.560
We also got tons of mail about the deleted cold open that I had shared about for this episode.

5
00:00:20.660 --> 00:00:23.100
It's where Michael loses all of the stuff in the toilet.

6
00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:23.760
Yep.

7
00:00:23.920 --> 00:00:26.900
It was in deleted scenes, and I wasn't able to play it,

8
00:00:27.120 --> 00:00:29.740
but it's been added back to the Peacock Superfan version.

9
00:00:29.740 --> 00:00:34.460
It starts with Michael screaming from the bathroom, and Dwight rushes off to help him,

10
00:00:34.540 --> 00:00:39.260
and then they both walk into the bullpen, and Dwight is carrying a bunch of stuff in a paper towel.

11
00:00:39.500 --> 00:00:40.060
Let's hear it.

12
00:00:42.110 --> 00:00:42.590
No!

13
00:00:43.810 --> 00:00:45.930
No, no, no, no, no, no!

14
00:00:56.230 --> 00:00:59.210
I do not want to talk about it.

15
00:00:59.610 --> 00:01:00.090
Unbelievable.

16
00:01:01.910 --> 00:01:02.390
That—okay.

17
00:01:02.570 --> 00:01:03.430
What happened, Michael?

18
00:01:03.890 --> 00:01:08.030
Oh, wouldn't you like to know what happened in the bathroom by myself, pervy?

19
00:01:08.990 --> 00:01:13.870
I—suffice to say, I had finished my business, I was just checking to make sure everything was fine,

20
00:01:14.450 --> 00:01:20.170
and my cell phone fell out and on, not in, but, like, on the rim, and then—

21
00:01:20.170 --> 00:01:20.670
It fell in.

22
00:01:21.070 --> 00:01:22.510
Just let me tell the story, okay?

23
00:01:22.830 --> 00:01:25.690
Jim, I knocked it with my knee, and then it fell in.

24
00:01:25.790 --> 00:01:29.570
And then I leaned over and looked, and my Bluetooth fell out of my ear, and that fell in.

25
00:01:29.610 --> 00:01:29.790
Bluetooth.

26
00:01:29.790 --> 00:01:32.570
And then I got flustered, and everything started falling in.

27
00:01:32.730 --> 00:01:39.390
My wallet fell in, my tip calculator, my candy corn, my white strips, all fell in to the toilet.

28
00:01:39.630 --> 00:01:40.710
And your keys fell in?

29
00:01:40.850 --> 00:01:42.810
I threw the keys in out of anger.

30
00:01:43.030 --> 00:01:43.230
Right.

31
00:01:43.410 --> 00:01:45.550
This cannot happen again!

32
00:01:45.810 --> 00:01:46.750
That's what you said last time.

33
00:01:46.810 --> 00:01:47.710
I know I did!

34
00:01:48.790 --> 00:01:49.930
Phyllis, this is not funny.

35
00:01:50.090 --> 00:01:51.010
This is not funny.

36
00:01:52.370 --> 00:01:53.590
Well, technically it is.

37
00:01:53.710 --> 00:01:55.550
Toilet humor, which you claim to enjoy.

38
00:01:55.770 --> 00:01:57.910
It is not toilet humor, it is toilet tragedy.

39
00:02:06.750 --> 00:02:07.230
Hey!

40
00:02:08.450 --> 00:02:08.930
Hey!

41
00:02:09.130 --> 00:02:09.710
You know what?

42
00:02:11.370 --> 00:02:14.230
This is the best thing that ever happened to me.

43
00:02:15.070 --> 00:02:18.410
This whole scene, please, you guys, it's so worth a watch.

44
00:02:18.470 --> 00:02:19.470
It's so funny.

45
00:02:19.710 --> 00:02:21.810
I can't believe that this was cut.

46
00:02:21.970 --> 00:02:24.750
I would have cut anything out of the episode.

47
00:02:24.850 --> 00:02:30.270
I mean, it's a great episode, but, like, I feel like more should have been done to keep this cold open.

48
00:02:30.470 --> 00:02:34.070
I say it in our breakdown, but I remember from the table read,

49
00:02:34.070 --> 00:02:37.870
laughing so hard when he says he threw his keys in out of anger.

50
00:02:38.110 --> 00:02:38.570
I know.

51
00:02:38.770 --> 00:02:41.010
Also, how much shit does he keep in his pocket?

52
00:02:41.370 --> 00:02:42.090
So much.

53
00:02:42.330 --> 00:02:44.110
How did the tip calculator get involved?

54
00:02:44.110 --> 00:02:44.410
I know.

55
00:02:44.410 --> 00:02:44.950
I don't know.

56
00:02:44.970 --> 00:02:45.490
I don't know.

57
00:02:45.690 --> 00:02:50.550
So after this, there is a scene where Michael comes out of his office,

58
00:02:50.850 --> 00:02:52.590
and he is holding a new invention.

59
00:02:53.090 --> 00:02:57.890
This is the invention that is going to save you from having your stuff fall in the toilet.

60
00:02:58.190 --> 00:02:58.410
Right.

61
00:02:58.410 --> 00:03:02.490
And you described it from the script when we first broke down the episode,

62
00:03:02.690 --> 00:03:06.230
but, oh, my gosh, seeing the footage again,

63
00:03:07.490 --> 00:03:09.530
Michael is showing it off.

64
00:03:09.630 --> 00:03:10.670
He's standing at reception.

65
00:03:10.670 --> 00:03:14.590
So I'm in this two-shot with him, and he's holding up his invention.

66
00:03:14.770 --> 00:03:19.590
And I just remember the first time I saw it, I immediately started laughing.

67
00:03:19.730 --> 00:03:22.190
This is something that Phil Shea had to make,

68
00:03:23.210 --> 00:03:26.870
and I had not seen it yet, and it broke me.

69
00:03:27.030 --> 00:03:28.430
Well, it's just so ridiculous.

70
00:03:28.630 --> 00:03:32.930
It's like the head of a tennis racket, but then the handle's been chopped off,

71
00:03:33.010 --> 00:03:38.370
but then it's like a dishwashing brush attached, but then it has a chain.

72
00:03:38.750 --> 00:03:39.230
Yeah.

73
00:03:39.410 --> 00:03:41.670
You know the thing you wash your dishes with, the brush?

74
00:03:41.910 --> 00:03:41.970
Yeah.

75
00:03:41.970 --> 00:03:46.610
Like, imagine that dangling from the top of a tennis racket by a chain.

76
00:03:46.770 --> 00:03:47.410
So I guess the—

77
00:03:47.410 --> 00:03:49.330
So you put the racket over the toilet bowl.

78
00:03:49.510 --> 00:03:49.890
Right.

79
00:03:49.890 --> 00:03:53.790
And you have to do your business through the racket threads.

80
00:03:53.990 --> 00:03:58.430
Yes, and then you use the brush because, as Michael says, it's self-cleaning.

81
00:03:58.530 --> 00:03:58.710
Yes.

82
00:03:58.830 --> 00:04:00.910
Which, I mean, it's you cleaning.

83
00:04:01.130 --> 00:04:01.650
It's you cleaning.

84
00:04:02.050 --> 00:04:02.410
Mm-hmm.

85
00:04:02.590 --> 00:04:03.030
Mm-hmm.

86
00:04:03.190 --> 00:04:06.130
But you clearly can only go number one.

87
00:04:07.790 --> 00:04:13.050
I mean, I would think, but it's just—it's so absurd,

88
00:04:13.050 --> 00:04:15.450
but it's also just one of the funniest things.

89
00:04:15.890 --> 00:04:17.530
I'm so glad it's in the supervan.

90
00:04:17.690 --> 00:04:17.930
Same.

91
00:04:17.930 --> 00:04:21.130
Okay, well, we also got this letter from Sandra P.

92
00:04:21.530 --> 00:04:22.310
Sandra says,

93
00:04:22.450 --> 00:04:26.990
Whenever I watch Job Fair, I find it interesting that the series starts with downsizing

94
00:04:26.990 --> 00:04:29.590
and closing branches and firing people,

95
00:04:29.650 --> 00:04:33.750
and now they are actively recruiting people at a job fair.

96
00:04:34.270 --> 00:04:36.050
Michael should have hired Devin back.

97
00:04:36.870 --> 00:04:40.090
I love this letter because I didn't even put that together.

98
00:04:40.450 --> 00:04:46.490
Yes, the whole series of The Office of season like one through three is just about downsizing.

99
00:04:46.510 --> 00:04:47.610
Are we going to lose our job?

100
00:04:47.830 --> 00:04:49.070
Stanford closes.

101
00:04:49.450 --> 00:04:49.610
Yes.

102
00:04:49.770 --> 00:04:56.150
We're constantly worried about losing our jobs, but now we're at a job fair.

103
00:04:56.150 --> 00:05:00.150
Yeah, now we're recruiting people to work for us that we can't afford to hire.

104
00:05:00.510 --> 00:05:01.290
So true.

105
00:05:02.070 --> 00:05:06.890
So, you know, in this episode when Pam has to go find a second sheet of paper,

106
00:05:07.170 --> 00:05:08.550
do you remember that whole thing?

107
00:05:08.710 --> 00:05:12.010
Like, Michael is like, bring one piece of paper.

108
00:05:12.170 --> 00:05:12.350
Yeah.

109
00:05:12.350 --> 00:05:17.710
And then somebody signs their name on it, so she has to go find another piece of paper.

110
00:05:18.370 --> 00:05:24.030
Well, she goes to her old art room, and along the way, she sees a photo of Roy in the trophy

111
00:05:24.030 --> 00:05:24.930
case in the hallway.

112
00:05:25.090 --> 00:05:30.030
He's in, like, his football gear, and it says he was all-city team, first place, 1995.

113
00:05:31.430 --> 00:05:33.430
Pam stops, and she looks at it, and she says,

114
00:05:33.530 --> 00:05:35.810
Roy, nine years of my life.

115
00:05:36.450 --> 00:05:39.390
Then she goes into the art room, and she's kind of looking to see,

116
00:05:39.590 --> 00:05:42.050
oh, my gosh, I wonder if it's still up.

117
00:05:42.350 --> 00:05:42.910
On display.

118
00:05:43.290 --> 00:05:43.870
Yeah, Pam's art.

119
00:05:43.990 --> 00:05:47.250
Some art piece that she was obviously proud of, and it's not.

120
00:05:47.690 --> 00:05:50.670
Well, I love this observation we got from Patrick R.

121
00:05:50.790 --> 00:05:53.110
in Boise, Idaho, who said,

122
00:05:53.270 --> 00:05:57.870
I always thought it was an extra dig at Pam that Roy's photo was still displayed,

123
00:05:57.870 --> 00:05:59.210
but her art was gone.

124
00:05:59.430 --> 00:06:02.150
They left up his accomplishment, but not hers.

125
00:06:02.450 --> 00:06:03.150
It's so weird.

126
00:06:03.150 --> 00:06:04.250
I never put that together.

127
00:06:05.430 --> 00:06:09.650
I never put together that, like, it was, like, this added dig.

128
00:06:10.050 --> 00:06:10.390
Yeah.

129
00:06:10.390 --> 00:06:11.270
And I liked that.

130
00:06:11.270 --> 00:06:13.310
I'm sure that was intentional by the writers.

131
00:06:13.310 --> 00:06:14.710
I missed it the first time.

132
00:06:14.910 --> 00:06:20.390
It's also sort of that, and I don't know if you guys had experienced this in any of your schools

133
00:06:20.390 --> 00:06:26.750
growing up, but I do remember our football team had the biggest budget, and our arts and theater

134
00:06:26.750 --> 00:06:27.350
did not.

135
00:06:27.510 --> 00:06:27.830
Sure.

136
00:06:27.830 --> 00:06:32.230
So, a little bit that, of course, of course, those trophies are still around.

137
00:06:32.610 --> 00:06:32.930
Yes.

138
00:06:33.110 --> 00:06:35.930
And also, like, you don't get trophies.

139
00:06:36.070 --> 00:06:40.190
There's no trophy case for the artists in the school.

140
00:06:40.770 --> 00:06:41.850
The debaters.

141
00:06:42.370 --> 00:06:42.610
Mm-hmm.

142
00:06:42.610 --> 00:06:43.910
Maybe the athletes.

143
00:06:44.350 --> 00:06:45.370
Best one-act play.

144
00:06:45.590 --> 00:06:47.090
Maybe there's a plaque somewhere.

145
00:06:47.470 --> 00:06:47.810
Yeah.

146
00:06:47.890 --> 00:06:48.750
Back in the green room.

147
00:06:48.870 --> 00:06:49.670
Or speech.

148
00:06:49.970 --> 00:06:50.310
Yeah.

149
00:06:51.750 --> 00:06:55.870
Well, finally, we got this letter from Jennifer M., who said,

150
00:06:56.230 --> 00:07:00.410
you didn't talk about Charlie McDermott playing the cool high school guy on the podcaSt.

151
00:07:00.750 --> 00:07:04.090
Did he act in the job fair while he was on The Middle?

152
00:07:05.410 --> 00:07:11.190
Well, first off, my apologies for not giving Charlie McDermott a proper guest star breakdown.

153
00:07:11.550 --> 00:07:12.570
I'm going to do it now.

154
00:07:12.750 --> 00:07:13.070
Great.

155
00:07:13.450 --> 00:07:17.970
Charlie broke onto the acting scene with his role in Frozen River, for which he was nominated

156
00:07:17.970 --> 00:07:19.550
for an independent film award.

157
00:07:19.710 --> 00:07:21.350
He went on to star in The Middle.

158
00:07:21.630 --> 00:07:24.650
He did 215 episodes over nine years.

159
00:07:24.810 --> 00:07:26.470
He even directed an episode.

160
00:07:26.970 --> 00:07:30.270
And yes, he must have been doing The Middle at this time.

161
00:07:30.530 --> 00:07:32.950
Charlie is now primarily a musician.

162
00:07:32.950 --> 00:07:37.090
And when I did my guest star breakdown for Trevor Einhorn in this episode,

163
00:07:37.290 --> 00:07:39.470
I mentioned that Trevor was a Scorpio.

164
00:07:40.050 --> 00:07:44.910
Angela, you asked me if I was going to mention the astrological signs of our future guest stars.

165
00:07:45.130 --> 00:07:46.210
I have not.

166
00:07:46.650 --> 00:07:51.790
But just since it's all in this episode, I thought I would add that Charlie McDermott is an Aries.

167
00:07:52.130 --> 00:07:53.350
Well, that's fantastic.

168
00:07:53.590 --> 00:07:53.830
Yes.

169
00:07:54.090 --> 00:07:55.810
Well, you guys, that's all we got.

170
00:07:56.010 --> 00:07:58.110
Please enjoy your second drink of job fair.

171
00:08:02.500 --> 00:08:03.460
I'm Jenna Fisher.

172
00:08:03.660 --> 00:08:04.780
And I'm Angela Kinsey.

173
00:08:04.880 --> 00:08:06.020
We were on The Office together.

174
00:08:06.020 --> 00:08:07.300
And we're best friends.

175
00:08:07.420 --> 00:08:11.120
And now we're doing the Ultimate Office Rewatch podcast just for you.

176
00:08:11.300 --> 00:08:15.840
Each week, we will break down an episode of The Office and give exclusive behind-the-scenes stories

177
00:08:15.840 --> 00:08:18.100
that only two people who were there can tell you.

178
00:08:18.260 --> 00:08:19.260
We're The Office Ladies.

179
00:08:23.160 --> 00:08:23.940
Hi, lady.

180
00:08:24.260 --> 00:08:24.820
And everyone.

181
00:08:25.040 --> 00:08:26.400
Hi, everyone out there.

182
00:08:26.600 --> 00:08:28.320
I'm so happy you're here listening.

183
00:08:29.120 --> 00:08:32.860
Jenna and I, someday we're going to come out there and take it on the road and meet you.

184
00:08:33.400 --> 00:08:33.840
Whoa!

185
00:08:35.640 --> 00:08:36.860
That's news to me.

186
00:08:37.040 --> 00:08:40.540
I guess we're doing it, though, because if Angela gets an idea, it's going to happen.

187
00:08:40.800 --> 00:08:43.420
I think we got to do one in Scranton, Jenna.

188
00:08:43.740 --> 00:08:44.660
Oh, well, that's a given.

189
00:08:44.920 --> 00:08:46.360
We got to go to Scranton.

190
00:08:46.620 --> 00:08:48.820
We got to do an Office Ladies from Scranton.

191
00:08:49.040 --> 00:08:49.360
All right.

192
00:08:49.860 --> 00:08:50.740
It's been said.

193
00:08:50.880 --> 00:08:51.680
Now it must be done.

194
00:08:52.080 --> 00:08:54.380
Lady, tell them what we're talking about today.

195
00:08:55.120 --> 00:08:59.000
Today is Season 4, Episode 17, Job Fair.

196
00:08:59.340 --> 00:09:05.340
This was written by Lee Eisenberg and Gene Stepnitsky, writers of Dinner Party, and directed

197
00:09:05.340 --> 00:09:06.760
by Tucker Gates.

198
00:09:07.340 --> 00:09:08.400
Would you like a summary?

199
00:09:08.640 --> 00:09:09.960
I can't wait for your summaries.

200
00:09:10.140 --> 00:09:12.120
Like, Wednesday night, you know, because we record on Thursday.

201
00:09:12.120 --> 00:09:16.160
I go to bed and I'm like, ooh, what is Jenna's summary going to be?

202
00:09:16.460 --> 00:09:17.300
I know you do.

203
00:09:17.540 --> 00:09:18.140
I know.

204
00:09:18.300 --> 00:09:21.980
You try to text me and get me to tell you my summaries ahead of time, and I say you're

205
00:09:21.980 --> 00:09:23.400
just going to have to wait for it.

206
00:09:23.400 --> 00:09:24.960
Yeah, you want to surprise me.

207
00:09:25.160 --> 00:09:26.300
I go to bed thinking about it.

208
00:09:26.380 --> 00:09:27.480
I wake up thinking about it.

209
00:09:27.640 --> 00:09:28.500
Well, here it is.

210
00:09:28.620 --> 00:09:29.320
Wait no longer.

211
00:09:29.680 --> 00:09:29.940
Okay.

212
00:09:30.580 --> 00:09:37.280
Michael, Pam, Oscar, and Daryl attend a job fair at Pam's alma mater, Valley View High

213
00:09:37.280 --> 00:09:42.340
School, in search of the, quote, best and brightest potential summer interns.

214
00:09:43.100 --> 00:09:46.300
Jim is on probation at Dunder Mifflin.

215
00:09:46.420 --> 00:09:48.260
You know, he got his warning from Ryan.

216
00:09:48.340 --> 00:09:53.220
So he is going to attempt to redeem himself by working a potential client over

217
00:09:53.220 --> 00:09:55.440
golf with the help of Andy and Kevin.

218
00:09:55.800 --> 00:10:01.200
The rest of the Dunder Mifflin employees take the day off, despite a warning from Dwight,

219
00:10:01.540 --> 00:10:07.800
except for Angela, who ends her silent treatment of him when they find themselves alone in the

220
00:10:07.800 --> 00:10:08.260
office.

221
00:10:08.640 --> 00:10:09.400
It's perfect.

222
00:10:09.840 --> 00:10:11.200
That's a perfect summary.

223
00:10:11.600 --> 00:10:12.360
Thank you.

224
00:10:12.680 --> 00:10:13.340
You're welcome.

225
00:10:14.160 --> 00:10:15.460
Fast fact number one.

226
00:10:15.840 --> 00:10:18.060
Valley View High School, Pam's alma mater.

227
00:10:18.460 --> 00:10:18.760
Yeah.

228
00:10:19.160 --> 00:10:19.780
We got mail.

229
00:10:20.180 --> 00:10:20.920
Kavya R.

230
00:10:21.140 --> 00:10:22.040
and Courtney K.

231
00:10:22.460 --> 00:10:26.040
asked, is Valley View High School a real high school?

232
00:10:26.200 --> 00:10:27.240
And did you film there?

233
00:10:27.680 --> 00:10:28.280
And?

234
00:10:28.640 --> 00:10:30.400
It is a real high school.

235
00:10:30.780 --> 00:10:31.320
Ding, ding, ding.

236
00:10:31.620 --> 00:10:35.320
It's about nine miles north of Scranton in the suburb of Archbold.

237
00:10:35.860 --> 00:10:38.040
Their school mascot is the Cougar.

238
00:10:38.340 --> 00:10:38.760
Mm-hmm.

239
00:10:39.060 --> 00:10:43.740
And their school colors appear to be blue and yellow, maybe blue and gold.

240
00:10:44.040 --> 00:10:44.920
Goldish yellow.

241
00:10:44.920 --> 00:10:47.860
I went to the website, because it's the Cougar, right?

242
00:10:48.100 --> 00:10:49.200
So you're saying it's yellow?

243
00:10:49.420 --> 00:10:50.800
I'm saying it's goldy yellow.

244
00:10:51.200 --> 00:10:52.000
Goldish yellow.

245
00:10:52.700 --> 00:10:53.000
Okay.

246
00:10:53.360 --> 00:10:55.580
Their colors are blue and goldish yellow.

247
00:10:57.720 --> 00:10:58.320
Okay.

248
00:11:00.180 --> 00:11:03.040
We did not film at that school.

249
00:11:03.040 --> 00:11:03.820
Oh, no.

250
00:11:04.080 --> 00:11:08.060
We filmed at Birmingham High School in Van Nuys, California.

251
00:11:08.520 --> 00:11:14.120
By the way, in my research, I discovered that the music videos for Gwen Stefani's Hollaback

252
00:11:14.120 --> 00:11:20.420
Girl, Eminem's No Love, and Lil Wayne's Prom Queen have also all filmed at Birmingham High

253
00:11:20.420 --> 00:11:20.700
School.

254
00:11:21.140 --> 00:11:23.400
Very, very popular location.

255
00:11:23.820 --> 00:11:25.520
Well, wait for it, Angela.

256
00:11:25.760 --> 00:11:27.160
Do you know what else is filmed there?

257
00:11:27.480 --> 00:11:28.240
Oh, God.

258
00:11:28.400 --> 00:11:29.220
Oh, let me guess.

259
00:11:29.320 --> 00:11:29.720
Let me guess.

260
00:11:29.880 --> 00:11:31.220
Fast Times at Ridgemont High.

261
00:11:31.500 --> 00:11:31.800
No.

262
00:11:32.300 --> 00:11:32.760
Grease.

263
00:11:33.080 --> 00:11:34.740
It's an office connection.

264
00:11:35.480 --> 00:11:35.660
Oh.

265
00:11:36.180 --> 00:11:36.280
Hmm.

266
00:11:37.340 --> 00:11:38.900
A 40-Year-Old Virgin?

267
00:11:39.240 --> 00:11:41.240
An episode of Monk.

268
00:11:41.820 --> 00:11:42.340
Oh!

269
00:11:44.280 --> 00:11:45.860
An episode of Monk.

270
00:11:45.920 --> 00:11:48.200
What is it with The Office and Monk?

271
00:11:48.360 --> 00:11:49.320
I don't know.

272
00:11:49.620 --> 00:11:52.880
I really wish we had filmed back in, like, the 50s.

273
00:11:52.940 --> 00:11:56.420
Remember when they would do those crossover episodes and all of a sudden, like, Laverne

274
00:11:56.420 --> 00:12:00.320
and Shirley would be over at, you know, the Fonzie's house?

275
00:12:00.720 --> 00:12:01.060
Yeah.

276
00:12:01.060 --> 00:12:03.300
It'd be like Happy Days, Laverne and Shirley.

277
00:12:03.680 --> 00:12:06.100
What if we had a Monk The Office crossover?

278
00:12:06.520 --> 00:12:10.960
I wish we could go back in time and make that happen, because we clearly used the same

279
00:12:10.960 --> 00:12:12.740
locations and the same guest stars.

280
00:12:13.000 --> 00:12:15.400
Have Tony Shalhoub walk into the bullpen?

281
00:12:15.560 --> 00:12:15.960
Come on.

282
00:12:16.340 --> 00:12:17.440
And interview someone.

283
00:12:17.680 --> 00:12:20.280
Maybe Toby for being the Scranton Strangler.

284
00:12:20.580 --> 00:12:21.100
Yes!

285
00:12:21.440 --> 00:12:22.360
We did it!

286
00:12:22.620 --> 00:12:23.420
We did it!

287
00:12:23.560 --> 00:12:24.520
There it is, everybody.

288
00:12:24.520 --> 00:12:28.160
Your Office reunion is also a Monk crossover.

289
00:12:28.500 --> 00:12:28.840
Done.

290
00:12:28.840 --> 00:12:31.240
A little more information on the school.

291
00:12:31.460 --> 00:12:35.400
The school colors for Birmingham High School appear to be blue and white.

292
00:12:36.720 --> 00:12:43.280
Kent Zabornak told me that we had to create all of our own signage and props for the school

293
00:12:43.280 --> 00:12:48.860
because we had to make sure, per our agreement with Birmingham High School, that none of their

294
00:12:48.860 --> 00:12:52.380
actual logos or artwork or signage was seen.

295
00:12:52.860 --> 00:12:53.560
So there you go.

296
00:12:53.700 --> 00:12:54.600
We made it all.

297
00:12:54.760 --> 00:12:55.860
Everything hanging on the wall.

298
00:12:56.020 --> 00:12:56.300
Everything.

299
00:12:56.880 --> 00:12:57.440
Wowzers.

300
00:12:57.560 --> 00:12:58.240
That's a lot.

301
00:12:58.240 --> 00:13:01.840
But listen, when Kent told me that, as I was watching the episode, I was like, that's

302
00:13:01.840 --> 00:13:02.680
a lot of signs.

303
00:13:03.100 --> 00:13:03.360
Yeah.

304
00:13:03.640 --> 00:13:04.180
Check it out.

305
00:13:04.280 --> 00:13:06.600
Our art department was very busy this episode.

306
00:13:06.780 --> 00:13:07.280
They were.

307
00:13:07.820 --> 00:13:09.780
I'm moving us into fast fact number two.

308
00:13:10.020 --> 00:13:11.120
It's called golfing.

309
00:13:11.320 --> 00:13:11.960
Wait, wait.

310
00:13:12.040 --> 00:13:13.740
I sense a location breakdown.

311
00:13:14.160 --> 00:13:15.280
You are correct, Angela.

312
00:13:15.540 --> 00:13:18.480
And it's because we got a fan question from Sophia D.

313
00:13:18.940 --> 00:13:21.860
Where did you film the scenes at the golf course?

314
00:13:22.160 --> 00:13:24.140
Because I'll have you notice, I looked.

315
00:13:24.140 --> 00:13:27.540
We never see a sign for where our guys are supposed to be.

316
00:13:28.220 --> 00:13:33.600
I Googled, there is a country club of Scranton that offers golf, as well as a few other golf

317
00:13:33.600 --> 00:13:35.020
courses near the Scranton area.

318
00:13:35.020 --> 00:13:37.720
I don't know which course this is supposed to be.

319
00:13:37.720 --> 00:13:42.560
But we filmed at Vista Valencia golf course in Santa Clarita.

320
00:13:43.440 --> 00:13:45.740
It's a 27-hole facility.

321
00:13:45.740 --> 00:13:51.760
It has an 18-hole par 61 course and a 9-hole par 3 course.

322
00:13:51.980 --> 00:13:53.780
Now, here's what I found very interesting.

323
00:13:53.980 --> 00:13:55.100
Maybe only to me.

324
00:13:55.480 --> 00:13:56.320
Let's hear it.

325
00:13:56.320 --> 00:14:01.380
The prices to play depend on what day you're playing and also what time you arrive.

326
00:14:01.700 --> 00:14:05.640
It's least expensive to go during the week in the afternoon.

327
00:14:05.940 --> 00:14:10.600
If you come first thing in the morning, it's going to cost you $24.50 to walk the course

328
00:14:10.600 --> 00:14:12.460
or $36.50 to ride it.

329
00:14:12.580 --> 00:14:18.060
If you come at 3 o'clock, it's only $13 to walk it and $23.50 to ride it.

330
00:14:18.200 --> 00:14:21.220
But why is it more expensive to ride it?

331
00:14:21.300 --> 00:14:22.740
Is it because it comes with the cart?

332
00:14:22.920 --> 00:14:24.240
I couldn't find that information.

333
00:14:24.240 --> 00:14:29.340
It seems like you'd flow faster if you're riding it than if you're walking it.

334
00:14:29.600 --> 00:14:30.360
Guess what, everybody?

335
00:14:30.520 --> 00:14:31.780
I don't know a lot about golfing.

336
00:14:33.020 --> 00:14:35.480
This is why I'm quiet because I'm like, I don't know.

337
00:14:35.780 --> 00:14:37.400
But here's the big kicker.

338
00:14:37.500 --> 00:14:40.000
And this is why I think you and I need to go to this golf course.

339
00:14:40.240 --> 00:14:40.520
Okay.

340
00:14:40.920 --> 00:14:42.920
They have something called foot golf.

341
00:14:43.240 --> 00:14:44.080
Foot golf?

342
00:14:44.400 --> 00:14:45.680
I'd never heard of it.

343
00:14:45.820 --> 00:14:46.860
It's a real thing.

344
00:14:47.020 --> 00:14:49.660
It's a combination of soccer and golf.

345
00:14:49.980 --> 00:14:50.900
And hacky sack.

346
00:14:51.360 --> 00:14:53.460
I think you could hacky and sack it in there.

347
00:14:53.460 --> 00:14:58.800
There's basically a special golf course, but the holes are really big and you kick the

348
00:14:58.800 --> 00:15:00.800
ball down the course into the hole.

349
00:15:01.200 --> 00:15:01.540
Okay.

350
00:15:02.020 --> 00:15:02.480
Foot golf.

351
00:15:02.880 --> 00:15:05.360
Maybe we could frolf and then foot golf.

352
00:15:05.780 --> 00:15:10.620
I would foot golf if there was like a pony keg set up on like the eighth hole.

353
00:15:10.760 --> 00:15:14.700
So like you kick your ball, then you have a beer, then you kick your ball.

354
00:15:14.820 --> 00:15:16.020
What's a pony keg?

355
00:15:16.120 --> 00:15:16.880
A pony keg?

356
00:15:17.020 --> 00:15:17.280
Isn't that?

357
00:15:17.400 --> 00:15:18.620
Don't y'all have pony kegs?

358
00:15:18.760 --> 00:15:19.500
It's like a party keg.

359
00:15:19.620 --> 00:15:21.140
It's like a mini keg of beer.

360
00:15:21.140 --> 00:15:22.000
A pony keg?

361
00:15:22.120 --> 00:15:22.320
Anyone?

362
00:15:22.940 --> 00:15:23.380
Sam?

363
00:15:23.660 --> 00:15:24.100
Cassie?

364
00:15:24.240 --> 00:15:24.720
Pony keg?

365
00:15:24.800 --> 00:15:25.320
Ever heard of it?

366
00:15:26.120 --> 00:15:28.040
A pony keg is a mini keg?

367
00:15:28.240 --> 00:15:28.680
Yeah.

368
00:15:28.860 --> 00:15:29.840
It's like a baby keg.

369
00:15:29.900 --> 00:15:30.400
No, you're right.

370
00:15:30.460 --> 00:15:31.860
Pony keg is a quarter keg.

371
00:15:31.920 --> 00:15:32.160
Yeah!

372
00:15:32.400 --> 00:15:33.060
Thank you!

373
00:15:33.700 --> 00:15:35.160
What's a half keg called?

374
00:15:37.390 --> 00:15:37.830
Silence.

375
00:15:41.920 --> 00:15:43.560
I don't find any cool names.

376
00:15:44.080 --> 00:15:44.360
Oh.

377
00:15:44.800 --> 00:15:45.840
So you can get up...

378
00:15:45.840 --> 00:15:46.680
Here are your choices.

379
00:15:46.940 --> 00:15:48.760
Pony keg, half keg, keg.

380
00:15:49.960 --> 00:15:50.400
Hmm.

381
00:15:51.140 --> 00:15:55.420
I feel like they sell more pony kegs just because the name is cute, but I don't know.

382
00:15:55.420 --> 00:15:59.120
And you can carry them if you're on the petite side, like myself.

383
00:15:59.760 --> 00:16:01.460
Oh, we're learning so much today.

384
00:16:01.600 --> 00:16:02.280
So much.

385
00:16:02.840 --> 00:16:04.120
Fast fact number three.

386
00:16:04.460 --> 00:16:09.400
Angela, you were very, very, very pregnant in this episode.

387
00:16:09.740 --> 00:16:11.300
Yeah, I was.

388
00:16:11.640 --> 00:16:18.020
When you were filming your scenes with Dwight in the office, Lee Eisenberg had the flu.

389
00:16:18.200 --> 00:16:19.160
He was not there that day.

390
00:16:19.340 --> 00:16:21.200
Only Gene Stepnitsky was on the set.

391
00:16:21.200 --> 00:16:25.360
When they got into the editing bay to edit the episode, Lee Eisenberg was there.

392
00:16:25.520 --> 00:16:30.280
And he said, you guys, why don't we have any wider shots of these scenes?

393
00:16:30.540 --> 00:16:37.060
And Dave Rogers and Gene had to remind him because Angela's belly was very hard to hide.

394
00:16:37.520 --> 00:16:43.220
So all of these shots are like Angela from like the shoulders up.

395
00:16:43.220 --> 00:16:46.280
But here is what else I found in my Googling, Angela.

396
00:16:46.680 --> 00:16:47.220
What?

397
00:16:47.680 --> 00:16:51.660
By the time this episode aired, you had given birth.

398
00:16:52.100 --> 00:16:53.020
I know.

399
00:16:53.400 --> 00:16:57.040
You gave birth five days before this episode aired.

400
00:16:57.380 --> 00:16:58.300
That is true.

401
00:16:58.720 --> 00:17:01.020
Well, lady, I have a really fun story from this episode.

402
00:17:01.280 --> 00:17:04.140
And it's something that involves the golf course.

403
00:17:04.140 --> 00:17:06.420
I had no scenes at the golf course.

404
00:17:06.420 --> 00:17:08.760
But I went to visit the fellas.

405
00:17:08.760 --> 00:17:13.860
I was doing a whole series at this time on NBC.com called Adventures with Angela.

406
00:17:14.420 --> 00:17:18.360
And Creed and Ed had written a song for my baby.

407
00:17:18.920 --> 00:17:22.140
I mean, with the banjo, the guitar, the whole thing.

408
00:17:22.380 --> 00:17:26.160
So I went to the golf course on Monday on their lunch.

409
00:17:26.160 --> 00:17:30.080
And we sat out in this beautiful, green, like grassy area.

410
00:17:30.620 --> 00:17:32.140
And they sang to me.

411
00:17:32.360 --> 00:17:36.700
And not only that, I couldn't remember how we got there.

412
00:17:36.820 --> 00:17:39.980
I was like, I don't remember driving to this place or where it was.

413
00:17:40.100 --> 00:17:43.340
And you know when you're a passenger how you don't really pay attention as much?

414
00:17:43.700 --> 00:17:43.960
Yeah.

415
00:17:44.700 --> 00:17:49.260
So I found this email that I had written to John Krasinski where I said,

416
00:17:49.620 --> 00:17:51.280
Hey, John, I'll see you Monday.

417
00:17:51.280 --> 00:17:52.180
I can't wait.

418
00:17:52.400 --> 00:17:54.500
Creed is picking me up in his sports car.

419
00:17:54.660 --> 00:17:55.560
Should I be scared?

420
00:17:55.560 --> 00:17:57.360
And we're going to come and have lunch.

421
00:17:57.500 --> 00:18:00.800
And he and Ed are going to sing a song for my little baby.

422
00:18:01.660 --> 00:18:04.720
Oh, so you rode in Creed's sports car?

423
00:18:04.980 --> 00:18:08.120
I rode in Creed's little two-seater sports car.

424
00:18:08.460 --> 00:18:10.420
And they sang this song to me.

425
00:18:10.460 --> 00:18:12.160
And it was on NBC.com.

426
00:18:12.280 --> 00:18:13.480
And Jenna, they gave me a copy.

427
00:18:13.540 --> 00:18:17.660
And I tore my house up looking for this this week.

428
00:18:17.780 --> 00:18:20.500
I have ransacked the whole house.

429
00:18:20.680 --> 00:18:22.460
I know I have it somewhere.

430
00:18:22.460 --> 00:18:24.500
And I really wanted to play it for you guys.

431
00:18:24.500 --> 00:18:28.860
But Joya, who worked with us over at NBC.com, is on the case.

432
00:18:29.060 --> 00:18:29.960
She's going to find it.

433
00:18:30.240 --> 00:18:34.540
And hopefully, maybe in a revisited, I'll be able to play it for you guys because it's

434
00:18:34.540 --> 00:18:35.280
really special.

435
00:18:35.280 --> 00:18:37.620
And I'm just heartbroken that I couldn't find it.

436
00:18:38.040 --> 00:18:40.260
That is so cool, Angela.

437
00:18:40.560 --> 00:18:42.520
I remember seeing the video of that.

438
00:18:42.520 --> 00:18:44.420
So I really do hope you find it.

439
00:18:44.580 --> 00:18:45.380
Me too.

440
00:18:45.380 --> 00:18:46.000
Me too.

441
00:18:46.120 --> 00:18:46.760
It was so cute.

442
00:18:46.900 --> 00:18:49.840
I remember Creed started off with, Angela's baby.

443
00:18:50.440 --> 00:18:51.960
It was just so fun.

444
00:18:52.500 --> 00:18:55.040
Well, and that's really all I had for this.

445
00:18:55.160 --> 00:18:59.560
I guess I have something that could be considered half a fast fact that I could throw in there.

446
00:18:59.840 --> 00:19:01.120
Half a fast fact?

447
00:19:01.260 --> 00:19:01.780
What you got?

448
00:19:02.080 --> 00:19:07.340
My half a fast fact is that Toby was not in this episode because he was busy writing the

449
00:19:07.340 --> 00:19:08.080
season finale.

450
00:19:08.560 --> 00:19:10.660
Ooh, that is a good one.

451
00:19:10.860 --> 00:19:12.640
Well, I have a little Kinsey tidbit.

452
00:19:13.060 --> 00:19:15.880
Ooh, guess who found her script of job fair?

453
00:19:16.460 --> 00:19:17.260
This lady.

454
00:19:17.720 --> 00:19:18.680
Oh my gosh, Angela.

455
00:19:18.820 --> 00:19:22.300
This is very exciting to me because I have a couple of fan questions that I didn't know

456
00:19:22.300 --> 00:19:24.420
the answer to, but I bet the answers are in the script.

457
00:19:24.720 --> 00:19:25.780
Ooh, ooh, let me get it.

458
00:19:25.840 --> 00:19:26.260
I'll get it.

459
00:19:26.340 --> 00:19:30.080
And let's go to break and we'll come back and jump into some job fair.

460
00:19:30.640 --> 00:19:31.260
I like it.

461
00:19:31.680 --> 00:19:42.340
All right.

462
00:19:42.340 --> 00:19:43.260
We are back.

463
00:19:43.440 --> 00:19:46.840
I have my script of job fair and Jenna right out of the gate.

464
00:19:46.840 --> 00:19:48.300
I have a question for you.

465
00:19:48.460 --> 00:19:49.200
What is it?

466
00:19:49.500 --> 00:19:52.940
Did you notice that this episode does not have a cold open?

467
00:19:53.240 --> 00:19:54.840
I kind of did, Angela.

468
00:19:55.100 --> 00:19:58.900
We have a scene before the credits, but it's on plot.

469
00:19:58.900 --> 00:20:00.060
It's on story.

470
00:20:00.300 --> 00:20:04.180
It's not one of those standalone comedic cold opens that we're used to.

471
00:20:04.320 --> 00:20:05.260
I did notice.

472
00:20:05.480 --> 00:20:05.900
That's right.

473
00:20:06.000 --> 00:20:08.240
We just kind of get right into the meat of the episode, right?

474
00:20:08.540 --> 00:20:08.920
Yes.

475
00:20:09.100 --> 00:20:12.500
There was a cold open and I'm going to read you a little bit about what it was.

476
00:20:12.600 --> 00:20:12.820
Okay?

477
00:20:12.820 --> 00:20:13.480
Okay.

478
00:20:13.480 --> 00:20:13.640
Okay.

479
00:20:13.940 --> 00:20:20.380
So in the cold open, you hear this screaming noise from the men's restroom and everyone

480
00:20:20.380 --> 00:20:22.780
in the bullpen kind of grumbles like, not again.

481
00:20:23.300 --> 00:20:25.240
And Michael comes out.

482
00:20:25.440 --> 00:20:30.240
He's just exasperated because he has dropped everything that was in his pockets into the

483
00:20:30.240 --> 00:20:30.600
toilet.

484
00:20:30.620 --> 00:20:31.540
Like everything.

485
00:20:31.740 --> 00:20:32.500
He lists it off.

486
00:20:32.580 --> 00:20:38.320
He dropped his cell phone, his tip calculator, his wallet, his white strips, candy corn, his

487
00:20:38.320 --> 00:20:38.800
eraser.

488
00:20:38.800 --> 00:20:41.060
And then Jim says, what about your car keys?

489
00:20:41.220 --> 00:20:44.060
And Michael says, I threw them into the toilet out of anger.

490
00:20:46.180 --> 00:20:48.360
And this leads him to this light bulb moment.

491
00:20:48.460 --> 00:20:53.940
Cause I guess this happens quite frequently for Michael and he goes into his office and

492
00:20:53.940 --> 00:20:57.920
he comes out and he's like, guys, I have invented this amazing invention.

493
00:20:58.080 --> 00:21:02.420
And he says, it's the mesh toilet guard to go over the toilet.

494
00:21:02.420 --> 00:21:07.140
And then the camera pans past him and he has just cut out the back of his desk chair.

495
00:21:07.460 --> 00:21:09.820
That's mesh into like a circle.

496
00:21:09.980 --> 00:21:11.180
And he's like, who's going to volunteer?

497
00:21:11.500 --> 00:21:12.380
This is going to be great.

498
00:21:12.620 --> 00:21:14.260
It's like, wait, portable, reusable.

499
00:21:14.560 --> 00:21:16.000
You could just put it in your dishwasher.

500
00:21:16.480 --> 00:21:16.880
So what?

501
00:21:16.940 --> 00:21:21.080
He's going to start using the bathroom through this meshy cover, but he's thrilled.

502
00:21:21.220 --> 00:21:24.200
He thinks he's going to be a gazillionaire with the mesh toilet guard.

503
00:21:24.420 --> 00:21:25.760
I don't know where to begin.

504
00:21:26.100 --> 00:21:26.640
I know.

505
00:21:26.640 --> 00:21:31.520
So that was the cold open that they didn't end up using and they just jumped right into

506
00:21:31.520 --> 00:21:32.080
the episode.

507
00:21:32.400 --> 00:21:33.280
Here's the thing.

508
00:21:33.440 --> 00:21:39.760
I can't remember if we shot that, but I remember that joke probably from the table read because

509
00:21:39.760 --> 00:21:40.800
we must have read it.

510
00:21:41.000 --> 00:21:41.140
Yeah.

511
00:21:41.300 --> 00:21:45.520
I remember the joke that Michael threw his keys in out of anger.

512
00:21:46.080 --> 00:21:47.600
That was my favorite part.

513
00:21:47.840 --> 00:21:49.580
So this isn't in the deleted scenes then.

514
00:21:49.800 --> 00:21:53.960
It's not in the deleted scenes, but it is in the script, but they didn't use it.

515
00:21:53.960 --> 00:21:54.720
Hmm.

